{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated","id":1477240,"title":"All the clans have committed heinous acts, yet the tremere are the most hated","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-24T11:21:42-07:00","id":1477240,"title":"All the clans have committed heinous acts, yet the tremere are the most hated","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It doesn't make sense to me at all, how come the tremere are hated more than practically every other clan. Sure they did some pretty messed up stuff, but the other clans like the tzimisce have done a lot worse, and were pretty open about it too.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">How did the other clans even figure out the gargoyles were former noseferatu, gangrel, and tzimisce? Like, wasn't their appearance completely changed, and weren't their memories wiped? There's no way they could have found out, unless the tremere told the other clans that they kidnapped vampires from different clans to make gargoyles.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I know the tzimisce had their pride hurt over having the members of their clan kidnapped, and see the curse as something sacred. But why would the gangrel care? Better yet how would they even know? Gangrel sires regularly leave their childer alone for a number of years as a test to see whether or not they can survive on their own. There is no way they could have found out that they were kidnapped. Same with the nosferatu, the tremere have auspex so there's no way they could have trailed them without getting caught, plus if some animal started stalking you, a vampire, you would realize pretty quick that that's no regular animal. Since animals hate vampires and all that.<br /> <br /> Not many vampires cared about the salubri either, while few did try to protect them, a majority could care less if they went extinct.<br /> <br /> If anything clans like the venture should be hated because they are known for taking over empires and using them to wipe out their enemies.<br /> <br /> Plus most vampires hate each other, no one would care if a rival in their territory suddenly died, clanmate or not.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-24-2022, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:24:55-07:00","id":1477241,"title":"","content":"The Tremere aren't hated because of the atrocities they've committed. The Tremere are hated because they've played the game better than everyone else and came out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> The Assamites hate them because they cursed the Clan.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce hate them because they stole their lands and killed so many of them.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel and Nosferatu hate them because they were used as experimentation fodder before taking a position as a High Clan despite being a bunch of Caitiff.<br /> <br /> The Brujah hate them because they're magocratic fascists.<br /> <br /> Or as Groundskeeper Willy said:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://preview.redd.it/tki17gy9uoa41.jpg?auto=webp&amp;s=879625558c7db302e5305f16ce26a736c4c17e6d\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:29:18-07:00","id":1477244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477241#post1477241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere aren't hated because of the atrocities they've committed. The Tremere are hated because they've played the game better than everyone else and came out of nowhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems logical, but if we went by the lore, the second the tremere were created, an alert was sent to every vampire in the world that they had to hate the tremere because they were usurpers, or something like that. Of course we would have to ignore that vlad tepes was also a usurper since he forced another vampire to embrace him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:30:00-07:00","id":1477245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477244#post1477244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems logical, but if we went by the lore, the second the tremere were created, an alert was sent to every vampire in the world that they had to hate the tremere because they were usurpers, or something like that. Of course we would have to ignore that vlad tepes was also a usurper since he forced another vampire to embrace him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh.<br /> <br /> Even then, that actually has an excuse because back then, the Tremere were ONLY a bunch of Caitiff diablerists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:34:54-07:00","id":1477246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477241#post1477241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere aren't hated because of the atrocities they've committed. The Tremere are hated because they've played the game better than everyone else and came out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> The Assamites hate them because they cursed the Clan.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce hate them because they stole their lands and killed so many of them.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel and Nosferatu hate them because they were used as experimentation fodder before taking a position as a High Clan despite being a bunch of Caitiff.<br /> <br /> The Brujah hate them because they're magocratic fascists.<br /> <br /> Or as Groundskeeper Willy said:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://preview.redd.it/tki17gy9uoa41.jpg?auto=webp&amp;s=879625558c7db302e5305f16ce26a736c4c17e6d\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>This. Coupled with the fact they possess blood sorcery which was made specifically to mimic the powers of the elders, makes everyone think, &quot;they're too dangerous to be kept alive.&quot; The problem is the Camarilla doesn't want to lose such a powerful assest, so the Tremere are pretty much free to do whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:37:15-07:00","id":1477247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477246#post1477246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Coupled with the fact they possess blood sorcery which was made specifically to mimic the powers of the elders, makes everyone think, &quot;they're too dangerous to be kept alive.&quot; The problem is the Camarilla doesn't want to lose such a powerful assest, so the Tremere are pretty much free to do whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But other clans had, koldunic sorcery, sadhana, necromancy, mortis, dark thaumathurgy, setite sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:46:41-07:00","id":1477249,"title":"","content":"The hatred of the Tremere is something you can't analyze solely from a Watsonian perspective because of exactly things like the retcon of everyone having Blood Sorcery that happened later in the game-line after the Tremere hate was formalized into the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T11:54:30-07:00","id":1477250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477241#post1477241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere aren't hated because of the atrocities they've committed. The Tremere are hated because they've played the game better than everyone else and came out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> The Assamites hate them because they cursed the Clan.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce hate them because they stole their lands and killed so many of them.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel and Nosferatu hate them because they were used as experimentation fodder before taking a position as a High Clan despite being a bunch of Caitiff.<br /> <br /> The Brujah hate them because they're magocratic fascists.<br /> <br /> Or as Groundskeeper Willy said:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://preview.redd.it/tki17gy9uoa41.jpg?auto=webp&amp;s=879625558c7db302e5305f16ce26a736c4c17e6d\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>A nosferatu in Russia wont care that 100 nosferatus were killed in germany. What I'm trying to get at is that most vampires wouldn't care that many of their clanmates were killed, because it takes time for information like that to travel, and many dont care what happens far away from them. Plus a modern age nosferatu, gangrel, and tzimisce wont care that a clan mate from 100 years ago was killed by a tremere, its not important in the modern age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T12:04:51-07:00","id":1477252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477247#post1477247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But other clans had, koldunic sorcery, sadhana, necromancy, mortis, dark thaumathurgy, setite sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those are out of clan for almost everyone, requiring insane levels of effort to learn at all, represent in game as experience. This and the fact most vampires studied sorceries at the time for ascension based reasons, resulted in few sorcerers that actually did much politically. Heck, the Cappidocians, the most political of such sorcerers, were the least political of the main 13 clans. Heck, Cappidocian at the time was just studying life and death in a cave, trying to become like God, or supposedly eat God.<br /> <br /> Tremere were an entire clan that not only were very politically active, but also innately learned a blood sorcery. This made them prime targets in the dark ages, as everyone wanted to learn their secrets, which prompted the creation of Gargoyles.<br /> <br /> Politics and sorcery make people distrust you, and the Tremere became the best example of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T12:19:40-07:00","id":1477255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477250#post1477250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A nosferatu in Russia wont care that 100 nosferatus were killed in germany. What I'm trying to get at is that most vampires wouldn't care that many of their clanmates were killed, because it takes time for information like that to travel, and many dont care what happens far away from them. Plus a modern age nosferatu, gangrel, and tzimisce wont care that a clan mate from 100 years ago was killed by a tremere, its not important in the modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its important to note that at least most vampires give a nod toward performative outrage. The Prince will talk at great length about evils of diablerie, the abomination of violating the Masquerade, and the importance of lineage. In truth, most vampires wouldn't care about the Tremere but they certainly are happy to shit talk them if it makes them look better as well as discourages people from following their path.<br /> <br /> In the Dark Ages, a bunch of Tzimisce being killed isn't a big deal and most people are happy.<br /> <br /> However, an entire clan VANISHING like the Salubri is still a big deal even if no one likes them. No one hated the Salubri either. That's some warning bells even then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T12:39:47-07:00","id":1477258,"title":"","content":"The Tremere were &quot;usurpers&quot;, meaning they are not descended from an Antedeluvian. The clan is around 1200 years old. Seems old to us, but the other clans date back to 8000 years or more. There are still plenty of elders around who remember a time when there weren't any Tremere at all. <br /> <br /> The analogy to Dracula isn't a match. No matter the temerity and arrogance of the mortal, his sire and its lineage were still vampires. The Tremere line though was seen as unnatural in itself, creating feelings of disgust we might feel towards the creations of Dr Moreau. People didn't see Moreau's Beast Folk as really the same beings as human beings, and neither did the vampires truly think the Tremere were actually &quot;real&quot; vampires. (Also see the creature of Dr Frakenstein.) Their origin tainted them. They were something else. Some obscene experiment.<br /> <br /> The creation of the clan was thus a complete shock, and they weren't accepted as a &quot;legitimate&quot; clan for hundreds of years, instead being seen as some kind of bastard, unholy monstrosity that had stolen powers not rightfully belonging to them. I would argue that at this time, the stigma associated with the Tremere was worse than with Caitiffs. Caitiffs were just bastards. Tremere were like some monstrosity that only seemed to be vampires. That reputation was only confirmed when the Tremere did all those acts you mentioned - kidnapping and experimenting on legitimate clans, waging war and taking land that seemed to have belonged to other vampires since time immemorial, developing magical power far in excess to what others had done, and so on. It meant the fear and disgust others had at the Tremere's strange origins were justified. It really wasn't until the founding of the Camarilla that the Tremere went from outcasts to acceptable members of vampire society. <br /> <br /> But even having improved their status, that reputation still carried over. Sires from the previous era instructed their childer to not trust them, and those childer saw all the other vampires and clans tell their childer the same thing. And when they saw that the Tremere clan was tightly knit and hostile to outsiders, this caution seemed justified. So they taught their childer that too, and so on. And so even while the Tremere are now seen as just another clan, there's still a bad reputation associated with them as a legacy of that era even if most vampires don't truly understand why that is.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's a strong argument to make that without the turmoil of the Anarch Revolt, and the Tremere's abilities to help the elders reimpose stability on vampire society, that'd they'd still not be truly accepted as legitimate vampires today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T14:22:08-07:00","id":1477270,"title":"","content":"As others have mentioned, the first Tremere were Johnny-come-latelies who upset the medieval social order and just declared themselves a force to be reckoned with from out of nowhere. They went from being just a mortal wizard cult to taking down a clan founder who had been walking the Earth since before the Flood while he was most vulnerable, in what would have seemed like the blink of an eye. They set the precedent that proved to the founders of the Sabbat that it could be done. The offense that the oldest and most paranoid and hidebound of elders of the other clans would have taken at this rocking of the boat has had nearly a thousand years to trickle down to the level of tonight's neonates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 03-24-2022, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T16:44:03-07:00","id":1477283,"title":"","content":"Claiming &quot;shouldn't people actually hate the Ventrue?&quot; misses the point that, actually, yeah, a lot of people hate the Ventrue. They tend to just be tolerated because few other vampires are willing to put as much work into cleaning up the messes of other vampires, or are as organized to do it, as the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Also, the claim that a genocidal alarm bell was set off the second the Tremere came into existence is a gross exaggeration. At first, the Tzimisce were the only ones who actively hated them; pretty much everyone else just held them in extreme contempt, which is just as dangerous in Kindred society because it means you're disposable. The Gangrel and the Nosferatu came on board when the experimentation on their kin was revealed. Not everyone hated them, just the local Tzimisce, Gangrel, and Nosferatu. Notably, the Ventrue actively allied with the Tremere relatively early on, which is a big part of why they are the two main pillars of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> PS: Forgot to mention, the mostly like answer to &quot;how did people find out how the Gargoyles were made&quot; is probably Auspex and Lots of Torture, since the Tzimisce were probably the ones to uncover it. A Nosferatu digging into the matter seems the other possible answer, since intelligence-gathering is one of their schticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 03-24-2022, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T17:14:05-07:00","id":1477286,"title":"","content":"V20's &quot;Lore of the Clans&quot; has a really funny line about the pest control problems the Tremere must have had on their hands after having made enemies out of Tzimisce, the Nosferatu, and the Gangrel - all of whom specialize in the use of Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T17:31:55-07:00","id":1477288,"title":"","content":"In addition to the reasons others have stated, the Tremere also truly acted as a clan. Sure, individual Ventrue were hated, but the clan as a whole doesn't get that much hate because they don't really act as a clan. The Nos are unified, but not aggressive about it. The Assamites mostly stuck to a small territory with the occasional individual venturing out and getting hired as an assassin. The Brujah were a random mess of individuals. The Gangrel....HAHAHAHAH!!! The Tremere were behaving in a frighteningly unified and aggressive way. The Tremere weren't a collection of individuals with individual ambitions, they were an empire of sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T17:43:18-07:00","id":1477290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477283#post1477283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everyone hated them, just the local Tzimisce, Gangrel, and Nosferatu. Notably, the Ventrue actively allied with the Tremere relatively early on, which is a big part of why they are the two main pillars of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the hatred for the Tremere was mostly relegated to Europe. Many vampires in other parts of the world could care less. But the Nosferatu would naturally dislike the Tremere - they have a sense of brotherhood and camaraderie that exceeds that of most other clans, even somewhat surpassing the Camarilla/Sabbat divide. Having their members, even ones in other parts of the world, get picked off and turned into mindless slaves would generally be something the whole clan would unite to some degree against. With the Gangrel, many of them would admittedly not care <i>too</i> much or would pick up and go elsewhere, but even with the ones who didn't care too much, I'd have a hard time imagining them getting too chummy with the Tremere, and it would be easy to take a stand against them when the opportunity presented itself. <br /> <br /> Really, had things gone a little differently and the Ventrue not made overtures to the Tremere, it would have been pretty easy for the Tremere to end up as part of the Sabbat (the younger Tzimisci probably didn't have much beef with the Tremere, they were blood bound by their elders and forced to fight them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T18:03:00-07:00","id":1477292,"title":"","content":"All Clans do horrible things, but the Tremere were highly successful and defeated many other factions. If somebody picks a fight with you and wins, you\u2019ll hate them more than somebody who picked a fight with your and lost to you.<br /> <br /> Though, I do think that the setting creators went way overboard with the factions that hate the Tremere and the ones that the Tremere had to fight. Mages from the Order or Hermes, Tzimisce, Nosferatu, Gangrel, their own Gargoyle creations, Assamites. It\u2019s too much, it just seems silly.<br /> <br /> I think I would have left out the Gangrel and Nosferatu. Having a conflict with them was just random and pointless. Then I would not have the Gargoyles revolt, keep them as servants aside from a few who broke free from Tremere domination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 03-24-2022, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T02:44:53-07:00","id":1477317,"title":"","content":"The Tremere are a sect as much of a clan. More like the Giovanni, FoS and Assamites. <br /> Only the FoS and Assamiters aren't nearly as organized and controlling of their members. The FoS are more happy to chill in the background, while the Assamites <br /> The Giovanni are organized, they're even more agressive, but they're nowhere near as competitive in the market as the Tremere: Thaumaturgy is more useful than necromancy, and fewer people envy necromancers as their practice is all-too-often pretty disgusting. <br /> <br /> The Tremere are closer to you than the independents. They don't have a dangerous ideology and can be part of the Cam no problem. FoS make great friends and business partners, but Tremere are great business partners and terrible friends. You're doing business with someone you hate but you often can't afford not to do business with them. See RL global trade for example. A lot of business is done with places we really wouldn't want to do business with if we had much choice. <br /> <br /> The Tremere aren't a clan that put great stock in being likeable. Being smart often leads to good social skills, Sure, and I'll grant that physicists in continental europe don't have the same social difficulties as they do in Britain or the USA, but Tremere like to recruit hardcore nerds that're happy to be within a rigidly defined system. If we look at character gen, your standard tremere is going to be a mental primary, and if he's a social secondary, the points would be far better spent in manipulation than charisma or appearance, the attributes that determine likeability. If he's a social tertiary, 1/4/1 is really optimal. <br /> <br /> Also players that choose Tremere often suck shit and grossly overestimate their intelligence, over-appreciate the spectacle of thaumaturgical power,, and will brandish the Tremere brand at any time they get into trouble with other players. It's easy to hate that. Plus a Tremere powergamer is going to be calling out spells rather than quietly rolling 14 dice like a powergamer using any other clan, so it's a lot more noticeable. I of course don't play Tremere like this because I'm actually extremely humble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T05:27:15-07:00","id":1477326,"title":"","content":"As a faction the Tremere predate the WHOLE OF VtM. Tremere the magus was actually one of the main villains played by the creator of VtM. That\u2019s why they are so central in the game background, and especially in its earlier editions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T16:50:12-07:00","id":1477373,"title":"","content":"Originally the Tremere were just the vampire wizard clan, no more, no less. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, the issue could be that the writers kept using the Tremere as an all-purpose plot device whenever new lore had to be back filled or a new situation had to be explained. <br /> <br /> Want to introduce the assamites, but need them restricted, just add Tremere.<br /> Want to rewrite the assamite clan weakness, just add Tremere<br /> Want to explain the Salubri history, just add Tremere.<br /> Want a massive kindred war during Dark Ages, just add Tremere.<br /> Want to add Gargoyles, just add Tremere.<br /> Need a reason why the Kuei-Jin can't leave San Francisco, just add Tremere.<br /> Need a built-in plot point to crash that San Franscisco containment, just add corrupt Tremere.<br /> <br /> The writers eventually realized they couldn't use the Tremere for revising/explaining older lore, so they did the exact same thing with the Baali. Sadly, the various writers kept messing with the Tremere into the horrid 5th edition nonsense for the clan.<br /> <br /> So if I had to guess why people &quot;hate&quot; the Tremere, it would be due to the fact that as a starter ST the Tremere complicate the hell out of the timeline. As a Player, Thaumaturgy adds a whole hell of a lot of system bloat that you have to figure out, not to mention the ST has to keep track of power creep. Then lastly when in game since many people don't bother absorb all the bloated mechanics and messed up back story, they get upstaged at a critical moment by someone who did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T17:32:31-07:00","id":1477375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477326#post1477326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a faction the Tremere predate the WHOLE OF VtM. Tremere the magus was actually one of the main villains played by the creator of VtM. That\u2019s why they are so central in the game background, and especially in its earlier editions</div> </div> </div> </div>True, their fictional history goes back to the old Ars Magica RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T20:38:09-07:00","id":1477397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477292#post1477292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Clans do horrible things, but the Tremere were highly successful and defeated many other factions. If somebody picks a fight with you and wins, you\u2019ll hate them more than somebody who picked a fight with your and lost to you.<br /> <br /> Though, I do think that the setting creators went way overboard with the factions that hate the Tremere and the ones that the Tremere had to fight. Mages from the Order or Hermes, Tzimisce, Nosferatu, Gangrel, their own Gargoyle creations, Assamites. It\u2019s too much, it just seems silly.<br /> <br /> I think I would have left out the Gangrel and Nosferatu. Having a conflict with them was just random and pointless. Then I would not have the Gargoyles revolt, keep them as servants aside from a few who broke free from Tremere domination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its kind of funny, because that means the tremere probably are the greatest contributor to the metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T20:41:23-07:00","id":1477398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477373#post1477373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally the Tremere were just the vampire wizard clan, no more, no less.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the issue could be that the writers kept using the Tremere as an all-purpose plot device whenever new lore had to be back filled or a new situation had to be explained.<br /> <br /> Want to introduce the assamites, but need them restricted, just add Tremere.<br /> Want to rewrite the assamite clan weakness, just add Tremere<br /> Want to explain the Salubri history, just add Tremere.<br /> Want a massive kindred war during Dark Ages, just add Tremere.<br /> Want to add Gargoyles, just add Tremere.<br /> Need a reason why the Kuei-Jin can't leave San Francisco, just add Tremere.<br /> Need a built-in plot point to crash that San Franscisco containment, just add corrupt Tremere.<br /> <br /> The writers eventually realized they couldn't use the Tremere for revising/explaining older lore, so they did the exact same thing with the Baali. Sadly, the various writers kept messing with the Tremere into the horrid 5th edition nonsense for the clan.<br /> <br /> So if I had to guess why people &quot;hate&quot; the Tremere, it would be due to the fact that as a starter ST the Tremere complicate the hell out of the timeline. As a Player, Thaumaturgy adds a whole hell of a lot of system bloat that you have to figure out, not to mention the ST has to keep track of power creep. Then lastly when in game since many people don't bother absorb all the bloated mechanics and messed up back story, they get upstaged at a critical moment by someone who did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah it kind of odd that the tremere are used to add flavor to many clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T20:53:32-07:00","id":1477400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477397#post1477397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its kind of funny, because that means the tremere probably are the greatest contributor to the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s highly probable that the Tremere are the single Clan with the greatest effect on the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T21:51:09-07:00","id":1477405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477400#post1477400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s highly probable that the Tremere are the single Clan with the greatest effect on the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shhhh, don't tell that to the other clans, they want to feel special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T22:20:11-07:00","id":1477407,"title":"","content":"I think most Clans are pretty happy not being as &quot;special&quot; as the Tremere.<br /> <br /> *casts a gaze towards the smoldering ruins of the Vienna Chantry*<br /> <br /> Being the favourite chew-toy of the metaplot doesn't tend to be a fun spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T22:25:55-07:00","id":1477409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477407#post1477407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most Clans are pretty happy not being as &quot;special&quot; as the Tremere.<br /> <br /> *casts a gaze towards the smoldering ruins of the Vienna Chantry*<br /> <br /> Being the favourite chew-toy of the metaplot doesn't tend to be a fun spot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IDK, I would rather know how to make an homonculus than run really fast. Also vienna makes no sense, how did they get past all of the security?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T22:34:33-07:00","id":1477410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477409#post1477409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK, I would rather know how to make an homonculus than run really fast. Also vienna makes no sense, how did they get past all of the security?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I'm not trying to dunk on the Tremere here, I am trying to be sympathetic. I am pointing out that constantly being put in the centre of the metaplot has often not worked out for them. Being the explanation for a variety of plot developments is a lot of why everyone *hates* them, like when they cursed the Banu Haqim. Or has ended up putting them in the line of fire for some very ugly beatdowns, like the burning of the Vienna Chantry.<br /> <br /> As for the how, there's a grocery list of possible explanations. The Technocracy did it. The Arcanum helped. A traitor on the inside, with a grocery list of possible explanations for *that*. How it happened isn't really the point. The point is that is the sort of thing that being the most &quot;special&quot; Clan in the metaplot gets you. It sucks a lot of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T00:46:01-07:00","id":1477414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477409#post1477409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK, I would rather know how to make an homonculus than run really fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>A homunculus will not save you from a hellfire missile, nor from incendiaries. Running fast...probably won't either, but it'll at least give you a shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477409#post1477409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Also vienna makes no sense, how did they get past all of the security?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably actual wizards. The Tremere get Thaumaturgy; Mages are Mages.<br /> Alternately, high-tech humans.<br /> Alternately, both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27305-joanna_crone","name":"Joanna_Crone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T06:23:00-07:00","id":1477437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477258#post1477258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere were &quot;usurpers&quot;, meaning they are not descended from an Antedeluvian. The clan is around 1200 years old. Seems old to us, but the other clans date back to 8000 years or more. There are still plenty of elders around who remember a time when there weren't any Tremere at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>One point of information, Clan Tremere is about 800 years old. They became vampires in the 1200's<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T08:02:08-07:00","id":1477441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joanna_Crone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477414#post1477414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A homunculus will not save you from a hellfire missile, nor from incendiaries. Running fast...probably won't either, but it'll at least give you a shot.<br /> <br /> [/FONT]<br /> Probably actual wizards. The Tremere get Thaumaturgy; Mages are Mages.<br /> Alternately, high-tech humans.<br /> Alternately, both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see your point here, no one is going to see a missle coming, so no one will get the chance to run, it does not matter if you're a tremere, gangrel, brujah, toreador, or whatever other clan, you're, dead. Plus if you're dumb enough to get targeted by weapons like those, than maybe you deserve to get blasted to bits.<br /> <br /> Technology wouldn't matter because, if I remember correctly there are rituals for that, plus tremere have counter magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T08:09:32-07:00","id":1477442,"title":"","content":"Ignore this, wrote the same comment and dont know how to delete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-26-2022, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T08:10:35-07:00","id":1477443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477373#post1477373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, the various writers kept messing with the Tremere into the horrid 5th edition nonsense for the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>They lost their headquarters, leading council and ability to blood bond, then a lot of them ditched their organisations. The only metaplot they're leading now is their own. There's no evidence to speak of that makes them (deliberately) responsible for the Second Inquisition, the Beckoning, the Sabbat's rapture, the Anarch uprising or the entry of the Banu Haqim and Lasombra into the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 03-26-2022, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T08:17:39-07:00","id":1477444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477443#post1477443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They lost their headquarters, leading council and ability to blood bond, then a lot of them ditched their organisations. The only metaplot they're leading now is their own. There's no evidence to speak of that makes them responsible for the Second Inquisition, the Beckoning, the Sabbat's rapture, the Anarch uprising or the entry of the Banu Haqim and Lasombra into the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im pretty sure what Thoth meant was that the writers messed with the tremere by making them the weakest clan in V5. I could be wrong though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-26-2022, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T09:33:02-07:00","id":1477447,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree with Thoth, I\u2019m a long time Tremere fan and I don\u2019t like the V5 changes to the Clans. It\u2019s not about reducing their relative power or influence, in fact I think that they went way overboard in previous editions with making the Tremere overly important, but I think that destroying the Inner Council and fracturing the Clan removed much of what made the Clan interesting and gave them a really ham-fisted \u201ctake that\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T09:56:01-07:00","id":1477448,"title":"","content":"The Inner Council set them apart in organisation from most clans, but I don't see how a couple of new dissident factions makes them less interesting. Did they become less interesting when the Tremere Antitribu were introduced? Even if you can't stand House Carna as an idea, House Tremere is right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 03-26-2022, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T10:10:10-07:00","id":1477450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477448#post1477448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inner Council set them apart in organisation from most clans, but I don't see how a couple of new dissident factions makes them less interesting. Did they become less interesting when the Tremere Antitribu were introduced? Even if you can't stand House Carna as an idea, House Tremere is right there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They feel a lot more like a club than a mighty clan. House Carna would have worked great as a secret society within Clan tremere that focused on the study of pagan magic. Maybe instead of fracturing the tremere they should have introduced more secret societies within the clan. I feel it would add a good amount of flavor. Maybe have some of the societies within the tremere war with one another, like having the horned society (infernalists) go up against the Eye of the serpent (followers of set). And others form alliances because they are somewhat similar to one another, or because their specialized fields of study mesh well together, like the Rodolfo and Trismegistus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-26-2022, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T17:48:39-07:00","id":1477492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477444#post1477444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im pretty sure what Thoth meant was that the writers messed with the tremere by making them the weakest clan in V5. I could be wrong though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, though there is another aspect to it that just confuses the heck out of me.<br /> <br /> The Tremere clan were always portrayed as less numerous than the other main line clans. This makes sense since they tend recruit with an eye for the mystical and hunt down rogue embraces and traitors. Add on top of this the blood binding to the council and the fact that Dominate is a clan discipline and you would have a very tight knit lock step clan. The result being that the Tremere don't step out of line or out on their own much. If anything they like to hide in their chantries and stay out of the way. In other words they stay out of the limelight.<br /> <br /> But then 5th rolls around and it is decided the SI ignores the entire Giovanni clan despite it having an HQ and being heavily involved with organized crime, they ignore all the hundreds or possibly thousands of brujah being uppity across the globe, they ignore Tzimisce and their flesh crafted monstrosities, and instead cruise missile the Tremere HQ..... when the Tremere had a ritual for several editions that causes all records of a haven/chantry to automatically self corrupt, self delete, or get misplaced.<br /> <br /> Excuse me, waiter, yes I would like to send this retcon ravioli back for something better please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T19:26:23-07:00","id":1477503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477492#post1477492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>But then 5th rolls around and it is decided the SI ignores the entire Giovanni clan despite it having an HQ and being heavily involved with organized crime,</b> they ignore all the hundreds or possibly thousands of brujah being uppity across the globe, they ignore Tzimisce and their flesh crafted monstrosities, and instead cruise missile the Tremere HQ..... when the Tremere had a ritual for several editions that causes all records of a haven/chantry to automatically self corrupt, self delete, or get misplaced.<br /> <br /> Excuse me, waiter, yes I would like to send this retcon ravioli back for something better please.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni leadership was destroyed by the SI and the Mausoleum, leading to the capture/death of Augustus Giovanni.<br /> <br /> But yes, the Tremere Chantry in Vienna was targeted specifically for the same reason that Wolverine or Worf is constantly getting their ass kicked or they want the big wrestler to get an epic win. The Chantry in Vienna was a symbol of Tremere arrogance and invincibility for multiple editions as well as the most recognizable vampire stronghold in existence. They wanted it destroyed to illustrate to the vampire players that the Second Inquisition could be taken seriously and was an existential threat to vampiredom.<br /> <br /> Instead, a lot of fans complained about how humans could NEVER beat the Tremere and it was ridiculous the Inquisition was any sort of threat whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-26-2022, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T19:31:10-07:00","id":1477504,"title":"","content":"When you are not around, the Tremere sneak into your house. Then they move all the furniture by a quart inch, rearrange all your comic books, dog-ear pages in books your would never dog-ear, touch your dice (that is all they do to the dice) and lick your food.<br /> <br /> And that is why smart people hate the Tremere,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T20:01:35-07:00","id":1477508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477503#post1477503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Giovanni leadership was destroyed by the SI and the Mausoleum, leading to the capture/death of Augustus Giovanni.<br /> <br /> But yes, the Tremere Chantry in Vienna was targeted specifically for the same reason that Wolverine or Worf is constantly getting their ass kicked or they want the big wrestler to get an epic win. The Chantry in Vienna was a symbol of Tremere arrogance and invincibility for multiple editions as well as the most recognizable vampire stronghold in existence. They wanted it destroyed to illustrate to the vampire players that the Second Inquisition could be taken seriously and was an existential threat to vampiredom.<br /> <br /> Instead, a lot of fans complained about how humans could NEVER beat the Tremere and it was ridiculous the Inquisition was any sort of threat whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe in theory. In practice, destroying such iconic locations just makes the WOD less cool. Y'know, I play various Marvel and DC video games and one of the fangasm experiences I have in such games is visiting iconic locations like the Hall of Justice, the Legion of Doom, Stark Tower, the Fantastic Four's Baxter Building, the Batcave.<br /> <br /> And it's not like these locations being inviolate ever made the player characters feel invincible. No matter how tough the iconic locations were, when guys come after you with flamethrowers, the last thing you feel is invincible. You are not the Vienna Chantry. You are a player character who can get incinerated just by losing track of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 03-26-2022, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T20:27:24-07:00","id":1477511,"title":"","content":"Moving back around to the response of other Clans to the Tremere, &quot;Cred&quot; must be taken into consideration.<br /> <br /> If an existing Clan victimizes members of your Clan, it's like whatever. That's just the Jyhad. Only those close to the victim will care, the rest will at best add it to the mountain of reasons to hate their old enemy.<br /> <br /> If an upstart group, that aren't even &quot;real vampires&quot;, victimize your Clanmates, and then get away with it? That's everyone's problem. That makes the CLAN look bad. That makes the Clan look <i>weak</i>.<br /> <br /> And like any street gang caring about its street cred, vampire Clans cannot stand being made to look weak. Both for pride reasons, and because it invites further attacks from other Clans. Half the Jyhad is built, not on actually being unassailable, but projecting enough strength that no one would risk testing it.<br /> <br /> Whether it's the Tzimisce having their blood stolen to create the Usurpers in the first place, or the Gangrel or Nosferatu having their members captured and twisted into mindless slave monstrosities, they could not abide such attacks. Not from a tiny, illegitimate bloodline, with pretensions of being a Clan, that (at the time) weren't even half a millennia old. They HAD to be opposed, and on a Clan-wide basis.<br /> <br /> It's the principle of the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-27-2022, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T20:52:48-07:00","id":1477513,"title":"","content":"I would also like to state that &quot;hated&quot; is also a word with some context.<br /> <br /> No one liked the Tremere in the Dark Ages. They were diablerists, upstarts, Caitiff, and a bunch of guys who came out of nowhere to kill the Salubri Clan. I don't think anyone liked the Salubri Clan for being a bunch of holier than thou vegans (for lack of a better comparison) but some rando strangling the hippie next door is something you notice. Especially if he moves into said hippie's apartment and wants to show up at the apartment house meetings.<br /> <br /> However, while everyone hated the Tremere, it should be noted that very few vampires were motivated to DO anything about them. The Tzimisce and Tremere fought with some allies of the former but for the most part, the Tremere are just something most vampires tut-tutted about. It's not THEIR problem that there's a bunch of crazy wizard diablerists on the loose as long as that's restricted to Transylvania.<br /> <br /> Usually when Tremere show up in OTHER places, they're given snubbings and talked trash about. The Prince let's them in because you don't want to piss off this mysterious group of warlocks but its not like they wanted to attend the castle parties anyway. The Tremere in the Dark Ages are doing their own weird things.<br /> <br /> Its only when the Camarilla is formed that they're now forced to let them in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-27-2022, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T04:24:01-07:00","id":1477577,"title":"","content":"I actually think the Ventrue and Toreador rather like the Tremere. The Ventrue have always come out on top in their conflicts against everyone else (as far as they're concerned) and the Toreador simply don't conflict unless they want some amusement. In other words, neither clan feels like it really has anything to fear from the Tremere. On the other hand, the Tremere are naturally well behaved and have always sought out ways to be useful to the Camarilla. I don't think the powers that be care as much about sorcery as they care about the Tremere being adept at conspiracy and naturally graced with subtlety and competence. <br /> <br /> It's also interesting to note that, if the Tremere were &quot;saved&quot; by the inquisition, the anarch revolt and the founding of the Camarilla.. well.. the inquisition was started by the Toreador, the Ventrue were responsible for the Anarch revolt (as they were leading the elder faction) and the Toreador and Ventrue created the idea of the Camarilla. Looks to me like the three clans are thick as thieves.<br /> <br /> But also keep in mind that the Tremere, like any decent cult, use conflicts with outsiders to increase their own influence over their members, so they're actually likely to play up even friendly rivalries in order to keep control within the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T04:56:50-07:00","id":1477580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gothik_Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477577#post1477577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think the Ventrue and Toreador rather like the Tremere. The Ventrue have always come out on top in their conflicts against everyone else (as far as they're concerned) and the Toreador simply don't conflict unless they want some amusement. In other words, neither clan feels like it really has anything to fear from the Tremere. On the other hand, the Tremere are naturally well behaved and have always sought out ways to be useful to the Camarilla. I don't think the powers that be care as much about sorcery as they care about the Tremere being adept at conspiracy and naturally graced with subtlety and competence.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting to note that, if the Tremere were &quot;saved&quot; by the inquisition, the anarch revolt and the founding of the Camarilla.. well.. the inquisition was started by the Toreador, the Ventrue were responsible for the Anarch revolt (as they were leading the elder faction) and the Toreador and Ventrue created the idea of the Camarilla. Looks to me like the three clans are thick as thieves.<br /> <br /> But also keep in mind that the Tremere, like any decent cult, use conflicts with outsiders to increase their own influence over their members, so they're actually likely to play up even friendly rivalries in order to keep control within the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transylvania Chronicles actually states the Tremere did a lot to cover up that the Inquisition was their fuckup. Goratrix bringing about the end of the Knights Templar to loot their goodies is apparently what clued the Catholic Church to not just the existence of vampires (they've known about them a long time) but just how many of them were inside their ranks, specifically the Lasombra, and triggered an interior purge that spread out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T07:38:45-07:00","id":1477583,"title":"","content":"My joking aside, a couple of points.<br /> <br /> First, vampires are a race of sociopathic tetchy cannibals. They do not need a reason to hate each other. Hate is their default state.<br /> <br /> Second, I suspect the &quot;hate&quot; for the Tremere is something the clan founders passed down through mental powers and through the blood. The surviving and involved clan founders of the Lasombra, Tzimisce, Toreador, Gangrel, Malkavian, Nosferatu and Banu Haqim were all involved in the jyhad. They knew something was going on with Saulot, and then Tremere and Tzimisce but they didn't know what for the most part. They could not or would not act directly against the Tremere as a group of vampires, but they did send out bad vibes. <br /> <br /> I am excluding the Cappadocians (and Giovanni) from this because the Cappadocian founder was a nutter and Giovanni were not really a thing yet. The founders of the Ventrue, Brujah, and Ravnos were also uninvolved. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T15:40:56-07:00","id":1477598,"title":"","content":"Apologies if I'm just repeating something that's been said a million times, but my impression is that the Tremere are not so much hated as they are feared. <br /> <br /> They did something that should not have been able to be done. They &quot;stole&quot; vampirism, from a bloody Antediluvian. And they still have access to some form of sorcery, even if they lost their Hermetic arts. No one in V:tM necessarily &quot;likes&quot; each other (generalization) but Tremere have literally done (or at least appeared to have done) something only the Giovanni has accomplished. And the Giovanni had to be a lot sneakier about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T09:08:03-07:00","id":1560344,"title":"","content":"Don't mind me being a Giovanni for a moment. Twice. This thread also covered very similar ground:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/173201-why-people-hate-the-tremere\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/173201-why-people-hate-the-tremere\"> Why people hate the tremere? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/173201-why-people-hate-the-tremere\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/173201-why-people-hate-the-tremere </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In a previous thread about what canon thing people hate, clan tremere just keep poping up over and over. Why is that? I mean in theory they are awesome &amp;quot;Vampire mages&amp;quot;. I have never got bore playing a tremere with tons of power to choose. However i started playing vampire with V20 so maybe im </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T10:04:48-07:00","id":1560346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated#post1477240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:14px\">It doesn't make sense to me at all, how come the tremere are hated more than practically every other clan. Sure they did some pretty messed up stuff, but the other clans like the tzimisce have done a lot worse, and were pretty open about it too.</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\">[FONT=&quot;]<span style=\"font-size:14px\">How did the other clans even figure out the gargoyles were former noseferatu, gangrel, and tzimisce? Like, wasn't their appearance completely changed, and weren't their memories wiped? There's no way they could have found out, unless the tremere told the other clans that they kidnapped vampires from different clans to make gargoyles.</span>[/FONT]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I know the tzimisce had their pride hurt over having the members of their clan kidnapped, and see the curse as something sacred. But why would the gangrel care? Better yet how would they even know? Gangrel sires regularly leave their childer alone for a number of years as a test to see whether or not they can survive on their own. There is no way they could have found out that they were kidnapped. Same with the nosferatu, the tremere have auspex so there's no way they could have trailed them without getting caught, plus if some animal started stalking you, a vampire, you would realize pretty quick that that's no regular animal. Since animals hate vampires and all that.<br /> <br /> Not many vampires cared about the salubri either, while few did try to protect them, a majority could care less if they went extinct.<br /> <br /> If anything clans like the venture should be hated because they are known for taking over empires and using them to wipe out their enemies.<br /> <br /> Plus most vampires hate each other, no one would care if a rival in their territory suddenly died, clanmate or not.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gargoyles have their memories wiped at the moment of their creation, not every moment that follows. Over a long enough period of time, they can eventually develop a new personality based on their life experiences.<br /> <br /> Gargoyles who had served in the chantries of powerful elders would have been privy to the creation ritual after seeing it be performed on others.<br /> <br /> Also, while the other clans can be bargained with to share their secrets, the Tremere were notoriously protective of theirs. Even going so far as to deploy scorched earth tactics to keep the secret of Thaumaturgy out of the hands of non-Tremere.<br /> <br /> <br /> You have a clan with one of the most absurdly overpowered disciplines in the setting, who refuse to share that power with anybody else, and who's true loyalty is to their own internal pyramid structure above all other sects.<br /> <br /> Yeah, of course the other clans wouldn't trust them under those conditions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T11:30:28-07:00","id":1560349,"title":"","content":"The Tremere are hated because they forced themselves into Kindred society and upset the status quo by using magic to change themselves without being directly embraced.<br /> <br /> Then later they did what was thought impossible by Kindred society at large. Tremere himself diablerized Saulot who like all members of the 3rd generation are seen as godlike and untouchable. Granted Saulot allowed it to happen to serve his plans but they wouldn't know that fact.<br /> <br /> Then you factor in that the new clan learned that they had very few allies and used their organizational skills to survive and thrive in the future centuries. Most of the other clans are riven with internal conflicts and couldn't counter that.<br /> <br /> In some cases it's more of a social status thing then anything else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T06:04:56-07:00","id":1560484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477250#post1477250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A nosferatu in Russia wont care that 100 nosferatus were killed in germany. What I'm trying to get at is that most vampires wouldn't care that many of their clanmates were killed, because it takes time for information like that to travel, and many dont care what happens far away from them. Plus a modern age nosferatu, gangrel, and tzimisce wont care that a clan mate from 100 years ago was killed by a tremere, its not important in the modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rather a dangerous assumption: human history is replete with examples of feuds (Likes the Jacobites Vs the Protestant succession) being handed down to generations who had very little reason to care whether one old king won the game of musical thrones, yet took up their quarrel anyway (Albeit in a much-altered and sometimes outright mutant form).<br /> <br /> For example, the Glasgow Rangers Vs Celtic rivalry (Which has at times been dangerously violent) has only the most tenuous direct connection to the Jacobite era, yet the memory of William III is regularly evoked to ground it in something more than just \u2018Us Vs Them\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s also somewhat dangerous to assume that a single century is a remarkably long period of historic time - consider that merely mortal humans can live as much as a hundred years - especially for a creature that can very reasonably expect to outlive more than one century (and most particularly for those individuals who HAVE).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T12:05:40-07:00","id":1560489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1477250#post1477250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A nosferatu in Russia wont care that 100 nosferatus were killed in germany. What I'm trying to get at is that most vampires wouldn't care that many of their clanmates were killed, because it takes time for information like that to travel, and many dont care what happens far away from them. Plus a modern age nosferatu, gangrel, and tzimisce wont care that a clan mate from 100 years ago was killed by a tremere, its not important in the modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Nosferatu would absolutely care, because if 100 of them suddenly got wiped off the census, that probably means a Nictuku is involved.<br /> <br /> The entire reason why Schrecknet exists in the first place is to serve as an early warning system for the clan whenever one of those bastards makes an appearance.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu are one of the most tight knit clans aside from the Tremere. They fully realize the risk they pose to the Masquerade, and how every other clan would be relieved if they were to disappear permanently. So they stick together and pool their resources.<br /> <br /> Loyalty to the clan trumps loyalty to your sect. Camarilla, Anarch and even Sabbat Nosferatu have been known to cooperate with each other when faced with an outside threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T21:17:18-07:00","id":1560667,"title":"","content":"The Tremere aren't hated because of broad strokes of anything. They're hated because they're the kind of organization that works by making enemies.<br /> <br /> Warlock history as vampires start with a very serious problem: they are completely new to this party, yet they have to carve a position of power and have to do it fast for survival's sake. That means shaking things up a lot and with no subtlety.<br /> <br /> It also means not having the time to build alliances based on mutual interests, they have to be forced to happen fast.<br /> <br /> All in all, the result is:<br /> 1. They antagonized everyone, even allies.<br /> 2. They consistently employed extreme or bullish tactics.<br /> 3. They operated tightly as an org, not a collection of individuals.<br /> 4. They prioritized blocking threats over building any type of good will.<br /> 5. They focused on short-term pragmatism.<br /> 6. They built a strong reputation as a group that makes no exceptions, deals with minimal threats with extreme prejudice, and won't negotiate on other terms than their own.<br /> <br /> You can say that, in the end, the Tremere are hated by everyone because they deliberately chose to be in this position, their whole survival strategy being based on making others hate them and making sure everyone knows they are a monolith and will suffer no exceptions, no deviation, no member that won't endorse and reinforce all your reasons to hate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T11:25:06-07:00","id":1560789,"title":"","content":"Welcome back Monteparnas","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T21:48:02-07:00","id":1560803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1560667#post1560667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can say that, in the end, the Tremere are hated by everyone because they deliberately chose to be in this position, their whole survival strategy being based on making others hate them and making sure everyone knows they are a monolith and will suffer no exceptions, no deviation, no member that won't endorse and reinforce all your reasons to hate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a shocker that one of the most elitist houses in one of the most elitist traditions would be full of insufferable ass holes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T22:35:59-07:00","id":1560805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1560803#post1560803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What a shocker that one of the most elitist houses in one of the most elitist traditions would be full of insufferable ass holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it correct to say they're one of the most elitist traditions.<br /> <br /> That would imply legitimate dispute for 1st place, and many in the Order would think both ludicrous and offensive that someone is more elitist than them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T13:37:59-07:00","id":1560825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1560667#post1560667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere aren't hated because of broad strokes of anything. They're hated because they're the kind of organization that works by making enemies.<br /> <br /> Warlock history as vampires start with a very serious problem: they are completely new to this party, yet they have to carve a position of power and have to do it fast for survival's sake. That means shaking things up a lot and with no subtlety.<br /> <br /> It also means not having the time to build alliances based on mutual interests, they have to be forced to happen fast.<br /> <br /> All in all, the result is:<br /> 1. They antagonized everyone, even allies.<br /> 2. They consistently employed extreme or bullish tactics.<br /> 3. They operated tightly as an org, not a collection of individuals.<br /> 4. They prioritized blocking threats over building any type of good will.<br /> 5. They focused on short-term pragmatism.<br /> 6. They built a strong reputation as a group that makes no exceptions, deals with minimal threats with extreme prejudice, and won't negotiate on other terms than their own.<br /> <br /> You can say that, in the end, the Tremere are hated by everyone because they deliberately chose to be in this position, their whole survival strategy being based on making others hate them and making sure everyone knows they are a monolith and will suffer no exceptions, no deviation, no member that won't endorse and reinforce all your reasons to hate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, even the Tremere hate the Tremere. It's just, they'd rather stick together and hate each other than go it alone and get ganked. They seem to enjoy stabbing each other in the back more than your average clan, so long as it only harms rivals' power and status, not the clan as a whole. Then there are the defectors...<br /> <br /> From the beginning, House Tremere was riven by factionalism. Yes, you had the Conservatives (led by Etrius) and the Conspirators (led by Goratrix), but even within those factions there was further factionalism and rivalry.<br /> <br /> Besides all being at each other's throats and manipulating each other, they were also manipulated by Kupala, Saulot, and [Tzimisce]. And apparently they provide a neat cover for many Baali (who are their cousins via Saulot's stolen vitae). These parties got them to build Ceoris in Tzimisce territory, become vampires, slay a clan, enslave their own members, and turn Goratrix against his master.<br /> <br /> Then, according to V20 <i>Lore of the Clans</i> (p. 210), almost a quarter of the clan defected with Goratrix during or after the Anarch Revolt. Which seems exceedingly high for such a close-knit clan, but it tells us just how many Tremere hate the clan.<br /> <br /> Enforced blood bonds ironically have the tendency to make people hate you, even as you enslave them, which is why people like Lord Mendel defected. Of course, he was also probably tempted by access to rituals that were forbidden to him in the main clan (<i>Giovanni Chronicles II: Blood &amp; Fire</i>, p. 50).<br /> <br /> The Telyavs went it alone because they hated the pyramid so much and despised what they had become as a result of the Great Experiment. But some of them apparently loathed the clan so much they still preferred allying with Goratrix, who invented the Rite of Usurpation, because at least he offered a route to empowerment (<i>Ashen Cults</i>, p. 55). This is presumably why some of them survive as ersatz Tremere <i>antitribu</i> in V20.<br /> <br /> In V5, they fractured into Houses Tremere, Carna, Ipsissimus and Goratrix, which is one of the developments that makes the most sense. I'm only surprised it wasn't seven houses (or more).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T16:10:34-07:00","id":1560837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1560825#post1560825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enforced blood bonds ironically have the tendency to make people hate you, even as you enslave them,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this phrase best sums up it.<br /> <br /> Not because that's all that happened of importance, but because it is the most didactic demonstration of their MO, and this MO applies to everything.<br /> <br /> Their namesake built the Tremere from the very beginning with those two assumptions:<br /> 1. Gather total, complete, absolute loyalty; and<br /> 2. Give no room for betrayal.<br /> <br /> He was personally good at inspiring love. A thousand years ago the Inner Circle loved him. But this doesn't extend to the organization and love really isn't in their checklists.<br /> <br /> They move in, make themselves indispensable, make sure everyone knows that, rinse and repeat. Take it by the Banu Haqim Curse: for centuries Tremere diplomacy was &quot;hear us, not only you owe us, we can still unleash the murderous bloodthirsty assassins&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T04:20:18-07:00","id":1560853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1560837#post1560837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this phrase best sums up it.<br /> <br /> Not because that's all that happened of importance, but because it is the most didactic demonstration of their MO, and this MO applies to everything.<br /> <br /> Their namesake built the Tremere from the very beginning with those two assumptions:<br /> 1. Gather total, complete, absolute loyalty; and<br /> 2. Give no room for betrayal.<br /> <br /> He was personally good at inspiring love. A thousand years ago the Inner Circle loved him. But this doesn't extend to the organization and love really isn't in their checklists.<br /> <br /> They move in, make themselves indispensable, make sure everyone knows that, rinse and repeat. Take it by the Banu Haqim Curse: for centuries Tremere diplomacy was &quot;hear us, not only you owe us, we can still unleash the murderous bloodthirsty assassins&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And not only does he inspire love, he then twists that love to his own ends. He was Goratrix's former lover, and at one point considered Goratrix his most faithful &quot;childe&quot;, yet he repeatedly sided with Etrius to encourage both parties to compete against each other. This led to great advancement in the clan, but also deep, deep resentment.<br /> <br /> Some of that was under Saulot's influence (such as sending Goratrix away to run France), but some of that was his own selfishness. By all accounts, Tremere was a tyrant who didn't bother hiding that he was a tyrant. He wanted people to fight for crumbs of his affection. Goratrix, on the other hand, presents himself as a charming rogue who's been done wrong by the clan, which means people are willing to flock to him, especially if they have no prior reasons to follow Tremere blindly (as the Inner Council did).<br /> <br /> But even Goratrix, who is probably the clan's most charming personality, is a conceited nightmare underneath it all. He can't stop himself from being a jerk either. Beckett describes Goratrix's autobiography, <i>House Goratrix \u2014 A History</i>, as being like &quot;a Tremere <i>Mein Kampf</i>&quot;. The Clan Novel Saga goes further and reveals one of his chantries is full of heroic iconography about him\u2014Goratrix as Prometheus, Goratrix as deliverer of the Fruit of Knowledge, Goratrix as the Lightbringer. Which says it all really.<br /> <br /> But that's what you get when a bunch of highly competitive, highly educated, elitist obsessives with very high Willpower get turned into Kindred. You only get to that point if you're arrogant to the point of delusion. Unfortunately, the fact they can mostly back up their arrogance just makes it worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T15:12:46-07:00","id":1560914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1477240-all-the-clans-have-committed-heinous-acts-yet-the-tremere-are-the-most-hated?p=1560853#post1560853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Clan Novel Saga goes further and reveals one of his chantries is full of heroic iconography about him\u2014Goratrix as Prometheus, Goratrix as deliverer of the Fruit of Knowledge, Goratrix as the Lightbringer. Which says it all really.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, that made me snort in amusement. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But honestly, the Tremere created one of the most hideously overpowered disciplines in all of vampire society, and then vehemently refused to share it with anybody else. A discipline which has allowed them to afflict entire clan lineages with a debilitating curse, and obliterate entire populations of antitribu off the face of the map.<br /> <br /> Of course they would be the most hated and least trusted.<br /> <br /> Would you trust an institution, if they were the only people on the planet who had access to nukes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}